Description: link the MusicBrainz C++ API as musicbrainz5cc
 Debian splits MusicBrainz 5 into the C library (libmusicbrainz5, no C++
 symbols) and the C++ one (libmusicbrainz5cc, where MusicBrainz5::CQuery
 and friends live); the legacy platform ships a single libmusicbrainz5 that is the C++
 library the sources use. Debian's -dev package ships both .so names, so
 the V\OS build links musicbrainz5cc.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: vendor
Last-Update: 2026-10-23
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@
 #	- 	if your library does not follow the standard library naming scheme,
 #		you need to specify the path to the library and it's name.
 #		(e.g. for mylib.a, specify "mylib.a" or "path/mylib.a")
-LIBS = be tag translation localestub $(STDCPPLIBS) musicbrainz5 tracker
+LIBS = be tag translation localestub $(STDCPPLIBS) musicbrainz5cc tracker
 
 #	Specify additional paths to directories following the standard libXXX.so
 #	or libXXX.a naming scheme. You can specify full paths or paths relative
